{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["וְיָדַעְתָּ כִּי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא וגו׳ — that is: and perhaps you will say, since He swore to our fathers to give us the land, why did we need to keep His commandments — for He will do what He promised in any case? To this I answer you: if you do not keep His commandments you will not inherit the land, and He will not violate His oath, for this is His measure: He keeps and maintains the covenant and the kindness that He swore to the fathers to fulfill what He promised them, until a thousand generations — for that generation, whichever it may be, who are His lovers and keepers of His commandments. And this is what He said earlier and concludes His words: ״וְהָיָה עֵקֶב תִּשְׁמְעוּן״ וגו׳ ״וְשָׁמַר יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ לְךָ אֶת הַבְּרִית וְאֶת הַחֶסֶד״ — to you He will keep it and not wait until a thousand generations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:29.891710064Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}